        "title": "refactor(ci): restore LOC ratchet headroom",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nRecent source-delivery changes pushed seven already-capped TypeScript files over the LOC ratchet. `main` recovered by trimming whitespace and tolerating inherited drift, but those files remained at their ceilings and blocked otherwise unrelated work such as #106039 and #106010.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis moves coherent logic into focused owners instead of relying on blank-line removal:\n\n- Codex message-tool `final` schema projection\n- Codex agent context-limit and node-exec option resolution\n- embedded-run source-reply mirror/completion state\n- shared terminal-delivery evidence\n- message-tool description hints\n\nThe seven ratcheted files shrink by 175 lines in total, and the baseline moves down to the exact new counts. Runtime behavior remains on the same call paths.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone expected. This is an internal ownership/LOC refactor; CLI, configuration, message delivery, and Codex tool behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node --import tsx scripts/check-ts-max-loc.ts --max 500`\n- `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs` — 4,986 entries match\n- 628 focused tests passed across payload/delivery, message-tool, auto-reply, and Codex dynamic-tool shards\n- prior branch-patch Testbox run passed `pnpm check:changed` and `pnpm build`; two final Testbox retries failed before code execution when their generated SSH identities disappeared\n- exact-head hosted CI [29227625587](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29227625587) passed on `685f790f5a9988ce3d0055ad208689e4046cea9c`\n- fresh Codex autoreview completed; two claimed unused symbols were rejected because direct source inspection shows both remain used\n",
